==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ĕn-vĕl'əp}}, {{IPA|/ɛnˈvɛləp/}}, {{SAMPA|/En"vEl@p/}}
* {{audio|en-us-envelop.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en-uk-envelop.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} ''[[envolupen#Middle English|envolupen]]'' from {{etyl|fro}} ''[[envoluper#Old French|envoluper]]'' (modern French ''[[envelopper#French|envelopper]]''), from ''[[en-]]'' "in" + ''[[voloper]]'', ''[[vloper]]'' "to wrap, wrap up"  (compare {{etyl|it|-}} ''[[viluppare#Italian|-viluppare]]''; Old {{etyl|it|-}} alternate form ''[[goluppare]]'' "to wrap") from {{etyl|VL.}} base *''vlopp-, *wlopp-'' "to wrap" of {{etyl|gem}} origin, ultimately from {{proto|Germanic|wrappan-||wlappan-|to wrap, roll up, turn, wind|lang=}} from {{proto|Indo-European|werb-|to turn, bend|lang=}} [http://www.wordnik.com/words/envelop]. Akin to {{etyl|enm|-}} ''[[wlappen#Middle English|wlappen]]'' "to wrap, fold" (Modern English ''[[lap]]'' "to wrap, involve, fold"), Middle English ''[[wrappen#Middle English|wrappen]]'' "to wrap", {{dum}} {{term|lappen||to wrap up, embrace|lang=dum}}, {{etyl|da|-}} dialectal ''[[vravle]]'' "to wind, twist", {{etyl|gml|-}} ''[[wrempen]]'' "to wrinkle, distort", Old English ''[[wearp#Old English|wearp]]'' "warp". More at [[in]], [[wrap]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{transitive}} To [[surround]] or [[enclose]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae V|4}}
#*: (''b'') sporophyte with foot reduced, the entire sporophyte '''enveloped''' by the calyptra, which is ± stipitate at the base.

